    "doc": "E-038 READ-OUT LADDER on the frozen anchor: is the pooled LINEAR ridge the limit, or the representation? probe_kfold reads a ridge on Z.mean(1) - 64 mean-pooled numbers - and the wind baseline is the SAME ridge on 2 numbers (section-mean tau_x, tau_y). At pentad those read 0.660 vs 0.670 (#390): two raw wind features beat 64 learned ones. head_probe=true adds the ladder top rung - a cross-attention head over the UNPOOLED ~67 section pixel embeddings - plus its matched raw-3x3 end-to-end control. Geostrophic transport is the east-minus-west difference ACROSS the section, which a mean destroys by construction, so this is the decisive test of whether E-038 headline is read-out-limited. At monthly the upper rungs were null (MLP 0.611 vs ridge 0.627; 5-segment 0.646) but the log states the reason as n=240 - pentad has n=1,459, so the negative is not inherited. EVAL ONLY: --steps 60000 = the checkpoint own step, zero training.",
